//The time complexity is (V+E)logV and space is O(V)
function dijkstra(graph, source):
    dist[source] = 0
    for all other v: dist[v] = infinity

    pq = min-heap with (0, source)

    while pq not empty:
        (d, u) = pq.pop()
        if d > dist[u]: continue

        for each neighbor v with weight w:
            if dist[u] + w < dist[v]:
                dist[v] = dist[u] + w
                pq.push((dist[v], v))

    return dist






Fibonacci heap theoretically faster,(VlogV+E)
Binary heap practically better.





