15.Standard Dijkstra marks a node as done once it is extracted with minimum cost.
But with a stop limit, the cheapest path to a node might use too many stops and fail later. A more expensive path using fewer stops might succeed. So you track (node, stops_used) pairs. A node can be processed multiple times at different stop counts. Each (node, stops) pair is treated as a separate state in the priority queue.
